To search for a Bluetooth device in the Arduino IDE, you can use the `BluetoothSerial` library. Here is an example code that shows how to search for Bluetooth devices and connect to one:

```scss
#include <BluetoothSerial.h>

// Set the Bluetooth serial port
BluetoothSerial bluetooth(9);

void setup() {
  // Initialize the serial port
  Serial.begin(9600);

  // Keep the serial loop open
  while (true) {
    // Look for Bluetooth devices
    bluetooth.search();

    // If a device is found, connect to it
    if (bluetooth.available()) {
      Serial.print("Connected to a device: ");
      Serial.println(bluetooth.address());
      bluetooth.connect();
    }
  }
}

void loop() {
  // Nothing to do in the loop
}
```

This code initializes the `BluetoothSerial` library and sets the Bluetooth serial port to port 9. In the `setup()` function, the serial loop is kept open and the Bluetooth device is searched for. If a device is found, the code connects to it and prints the address of the device to the serial monitor.

